  "summary": "Three preprints apply sequence models to somatic mutation, Cas9 repair and base-editing outcomes, each conditioning predictions on local sequence context.",
  "synthesis": "The shared thread is predicting DNA-level outcomes from local sequence context. EAGLE-MUT trains DNA language models on sparse somatic substitution data from esophageal adenocarcinoma and melanoma to learn context-dependent mutation probabilities. In editing, a large Cas9 study covering about 37,000 sites examines single-nucleotide microhomology in precision editing, reports that A-rich PAM editors are predicted better, and introduces the CRIfuser diffusion model. BEguided adds variant-specific guide design and comparison across 38 base-editor profiles, with BEguidedOFF for off-target prediction. What is new is the use of language-model and diffusion architectures, and of systematic cross-editor evaluation, for these tasks. All three are preprints, and the summaries do not report head-to-head benchmarks against established tools.",
